kosha swara-varga

  -- cluster for swara (note) concepts: shadja, rishabha, gandhara, madhyama,
  -- panchama, dhaivata, nishada — the seven swaras of Indian classical music.
  -- each swara is a specific frequency ratio relative to shadja (the tonic).
  -- the seven swaras together constitute the saptaswara — an amsha system.

  "sangeetham-varga-vishesa"
  "subanta-swarupa"

  -- sangati roots
  "spanda-matra-yukta"  -- each swara IS a measured frequency (spanda-matra)
  "matra-yukta"         -- swaras are defined by precise frequency ratios
  "avrti-yukta"         -- swaras repeat across octaves (avrti = repetition)
  "naada-yukta"         -- swaras are manifestations of naada (primordial sound)

